> You need to display wider content (by right-clicking a file) and then right-click empty space for narrower menu. It does not shrink until you open it second time.

Have not tested it, but looking at the code it can be an issue. I guess `OptionButton` should set preferred size in some other way instead of using `set_size`, maybe via metadata:

```c++
void OptionButton::show_popup() {
	...
	popup->set_size(rect.size);
	popup->set_meta("_menu_size", rect.size);
	...
}

.....

void PopupMenu::popup(const Rect2i &p_bounds) {
	...
	set_min_size(minsize.ceil());
	Size2 new_size = get_meta("_menu_size", Size2()) * win_scale;
	new_size.width = Math::ceil(new_size.width);
	new_size.height = 0;
	set_size(new_size);
	...
}
```
